  "body": "**Stacked on #333** (`issue/257-gcode-comments`, which also edits `tormach.cps`). This diff includes #333's commits until it merges; the #362 work is the last commit (55b7b83).\n\n## What changed\n`assets/posts/tormach.cps` gains `onProbeMove` / `onProbeRetreat` / `onProbeResult` in LinuxCNC/PathPilot words, so a Probe op posts on the Tormach mills instead of being refused by name.\n\n**The touch move**\n- It is `G38.2`. The control halts with an error when contact never comes, or when the probe is already tripped at the start, so the post writes no no-contact test of its own.\n- XY is positioned first, so a probe never starts from an unknown XY.\n- `G38.3` plus a `#5070` test was rejected: it hands that safety from the control to our own branch.\n\n**Reading the trip**\n- It is read from `#5061`–`#5063`. These are in the coordinate system the G38 ran in, in program units, so they compare directly with the expected values.\n\n**Back-off and tolerance alarm**\n- The back-off is incremental (`G91 G1 … G90`).\n- A deviation past the tolerance runs `o9nn if [ABS[#19x] GT tol]` / `(MSG, …)` / `M2` / `o9nn endif`, with a unique O-word per test.\n- `M2`, not `M0`, so the operator can't resume onto a wrong offset. `(ABORT,…)` is not in the stable LinuxCNC reference.\n\n**Setting the offset**\n- `G10 L20 P<n> X[#5420-#190] …`: the current position in the active offset, minus the deviation. It is exact in either unit.\n- `G10 L2` from `#5221+20×slot` was rejected: the reference doesn't say which unit the stored offsets use, so a G21 program on an inch-configured control could mix units.\n- With no offset to set, it writes `(MSG, CHECK PROBE RESULT …)` then `M0`.\n\n**Preamble**\n- A section at 0 rpm (a touch probe) writes no spindle start, no belt note and no coolant.\n\n**Arming**\n- Nothing is written. PathPilot's probe input is always live, and the probe type is a Settings-tab choice.\n\nThe sources for every word are in `docs/decisions/362-tormach-probe.md`: the LinuxCNC G-code reference, overview and o-code pages, and Tormach's PathPilot post-processor guidelines and G38.x pages. No other CAM system's output was read.\n\n## How tested\n- New `crates/app/tests/probe_tormach.rs` (7 tests). Goldens in `crates/app/tests/golden/nc/tormach/` on the 770MX (inch): `probe_face`, `probe_edge`, `probe_corner`, `probe_bore_centre`, `probe_boss_centre`, plus metric `probe_bore_centre_mm`.\n- `probe_op::the_tormach_post_probes_the_op_with_g38_2`: the op now posts on Tormach, where it used to be refused.\n- `scripts/gate.sh quick upstream/main` (macOS): post and app suites all green. `cargo clippy -p camcraft-app --tests` is clean.\n\n## Not exercised (draft until done)\nThese still need a run in PathPilot Hub (770MX), which the contributor will do:\n1. Whether preview stops at the first `M2`. In preview, probe moves report the programmed end point, so tolerance tests may read as failed there.\n2. That the G91 back-off right after a trip doesn't raise \"probe tripped during non-probe move\".\n3. That `o9nn if`/`endif` is accepted and `(MSG, …)` shows.\n4. That `G10 L20 P2` writes G55 correctly, inch and metric.\n5. That a trip during the plain G1 descent errors (relevant to #174).\n6. That G38.2 errors cleanly with no contact.\n\nChangelog: The Tormach PathPilot post writes the Probe operation (G38.2 touch, tolerance alarm, G10 L20 work offset) instead of refusing it (#362)\n\nFixes #362\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
